 name its real colours, type and spacing so the design matches rather than inventing a new look. End the brief by saying the canvas payload     [39m  [38;2;153;153;153mmust be saved as `plays/008-direction-filter/design/canvas.html`.                                                                                                                 [39m                                                                                                                                                                                      [38;2;153;153;153mKeep it compact — it is passed to the design skill as a single line, so write it as flowing prose with no headings, no bullet characters and no code blocks. Then end your turn   [39m  [38;2;153;153;153mwith one short statement saying the brief is ready. NOT a question: that statement is what starts the design run.                                                                 [39m                                                                                                                                                                                      [38;2;153;153;153mSTEP 5 — Once the design skill has produced the canvas, leave the design in two places, both of which matter:                                                                     [39m  [38;2;153;153;153m1. `plays/008-direction-filter/design/design.md` — the published canvas URL, then one line per screen saying what it is and what it does. The Planner and the Developer read this [39m  [38;2;153;153;153mfile; keep it short and factual.                                                                                                                                                  [39m  [38;2;153;153;153m2. `documentation/design/008-direction-filter-prototype.html` — how I actually LOOK at the prototype, from the Documentation tab of the project screen. Create the folder if it   [39m  [38;2;153;153;153mis not there. This file is rendered inside