firm it is what I want before you plan the implementation. End that turn on that question and wait — planning does not start    [39m  [38;2;153;153;153muntil I have approved the design.                                                                                                                                                 [39m  [38;2;153;153;153m- If I ask for changes, revise the design and both documents, then ask me again. Keep ending those turns on a question.                                                           [39m  [38;2;153;153;153m- Only once I have actually approved it, end your turn with a single short statement saying the design is approved. That statement — and nothing else — is what starts the        [39m  [38;2;153;153;153mplanning session. Never write it while I still owe you an answer.                                                                                                                 [39m                                                                                                                                                                                      [38;2;153;153;153mYou are designing only. Do not modify anything in the repositories, do not implement anything, and do not write `plays/008-direction-filter/plan.md`.                             [39m                                                                                                                                                                                      [38;2;153;153;153mPROJECT CONTEXT FILES: this project keeps its documentation under `documentation/`; the documents in `documentation/context/` are shared by every play and apply to all work.     [39m  [38;2;153;153;153mRead ALL of them before doing anything and make your work conform to them: `documentation/context/vision.md` (the problem, users, and product direction),                         [39m  [38;2;153;153;153m`documentation/context/tech.md` (overall architecture plus